    "source_kind": "measured",
    "note": "Found by testing what every earlier sweep could not express. Prior geometry sweeps used trail kind none with a fixed RR target and a short hold cap, which amputates the fat right tail this style lives on. With no target, a 4 ATR trailing stop and a long hold, median PF is 1.22 across five sequential yearly windows (4/5 profitable), while always-long and always-short controls on identical geometry fail in 0/5. Long alone wins 2/5 and short alone 3/5: the directions are anti-correlated across regimes and only the pair works."
